2.5 Mirrors, gazette cases, court judgments and Party regulations (added 2026-11-20)

    国家法律法规数据库 flk.npc.gov.cn, through third-party mirrors (lane cn-flk)
      flk itself is not fetched (2.2). Its own Word files and record fields are taken from copies others made, with
      no request to any host in China:
      - github.com/lawtext/law-flk-vol1 and github.com/lawtext/law-flk-vol2: the Word files flk serves (named
        <title>_<公布日期>_<flk id>), with flk's record fields (records.json: 公布日期, 施行日期, 时效性, 制定机关). No
        licence is stated on these repositories; they add nothing of their own to the texts.
      - huggingface.co/datasets/twang2218/chinese-law-and-regulations (Apache License 2.0; flk's metadata as of
        2023): publish_date, effective_date and status, used only where the mirror's record has none.
      The texts are laws, regulations, judicial interpretations and decisions of state organs: art. 5 (2.0). Each
      commit names the mirror file it came from and the flk record id; the official publication prevails.

    《最高人民法院公报》 cases (lane cn-spcgb)
      Taken from the corpus chengzi_h/chinese-law-corpus (gitee.com), read from its GitHub copy
      github.com/lttxzmj/chinese-law-dataset. Its curators dedicate their structuring to the public domain under CC0
      1.0 and leave out the editors' 裁判摘要. The judgments are judicial documents: art. 5. Each commit names the
      公报 issue and the case's page on gongbao.court.gov.cn, which is not fetched (2.2). The 审判长简介 printed
      after some judgments is editorial and is left out.

    上海市高级人民法院网 www.hshfy.sh.cn (裁判文书 of the Shanghai courts; lane cn-hshfy)
      robots.txt: none (404); no statement page linked from the home page; footer "版权所有 上海市高级人民法院" (read
      2026-11-20). No reuse terms are stated. Judgments are judicial documents: art. 5. Only the calls the site's own
      pages make are used, one at a time, at least 10 seconds apart; the rules of 2.1 apply.

    Party regulations (党内法规/)
      The Communist Party of China is not formally a state organ, so it is not certain that the art. 5 exemption
      covers its regulations. They are included here as official public texts, which the Party publishes itself for
      general application, and this note says so.

2.6 Personal data

    Official documents can name private persons. They are kept as published, except that in gazettes and local
    documents a private person's name or address is replaced inline ([姓名略], [地址略]). A document essentially
    about a private person is kept as metadata only. Court judgments (案例/, 裁判文书/) keep the text as the
    court published it; a full name of a private person that the court still printed is replaced inline
    ([姓名略]), and so are identity numbers, phone numbers and home addresses. Companies, officials, judges and
    lawyers stay.

